(function(E){ const x = E["exam-04"] = E["exam-04"] || {units:{}}; (x.units = x.units || {})["x04-s"] = {"id":"x04-s","patterns":["S1-frame","S1-food","S2-person","S3-education","TR-short","PARA-discuss"],"title":{"en":"Speaking","tr":"Speaking","fa":"Speaking (صحبت کردن)"},"objective":{"en":"In this lesson you will learn to take the whole Speaking test: answer questions about food in two or three sentences, describe a person for two minutes with real examples, and discuss competition and winning with a view, a reason and an example.","tr":"Bu derste Speaking sınavının tamamını yapmayı öğreneceksin: yemekle ilgili soruları iki üç cümleyle cevaplayacak, bir kişiyi gerçek örneklerle iki dakika anlatacak ve rekabet ile kazanmayı bir görüş, bir neden ve bir örnekle tartışacaksın.","fa":"در این درس یاد می‌گیری کل آزمون Speaking را انجام بدهی: به سؤال‌های مربوط به غذا با دو سه جمله جواب بدهی، دو دقیقه یک آدم را با مثال‌های واقعی توصیف کنی و درباره‌ی رقابت و برنده شدن با یک نظر، یک دلیل و یک مثال بحث کنی."},"sessions":[["explain"],["sets"],["exit"]],"explain":{"title":{"en":"Speaking: Parts 1, 2 and 3","tr":"Speaking: Part 1, 2 ve 3","fa":"Speaking: بخش‌های ۱، ۲ و ۳"},"objective":{"en":"In this lesson you will learn to take the whole Speaking test: answer questions about food in two or three sentences, describe a person for two minutes with real examples, and discuss competition and winning with a view, a reason and an example.","tr":"Bu derste Speaking sınavının tamamını yapmayı öğreneceksin: yemekle ilgili soruları iki üç cümleyle cevaplayacak, bir kişiyi gerçek örneklerle iki dakika anlatacak ve rekabet ile kazanmayı bir görüş, bir neden ve bir örnekle tartışacaksın.","fa":"در این درس یاد می‌گیری کل آزمون Speaking را انجام بدهی: به سؤال‌های مربوط به غذا با دو سه جمله جواب بدهی، دو دقیقه یک آدم را با مثال‌های واقعی توصیف کنی و درباره‌ی رقابت و برنده شدن با یک نظر، یک دلیل و یک مثال بحث کنی."},"stats":[{"label":{"en":"Time","tr":"Süre","fa":"زمان"},"value":{"en":"11-14 min","tr":"11-14 dk","fa":"۱۱ تا ۱۴ دقیقه"}},{"label":{"en":"Parts","tr":"Kısım","fa":"بخش"},"value":"3"},{"label":{"en":"Part 2 talk","tr":"Part 2 konuşması","fa":"صحبت Part 2"},"value":{"en":"2 min","tr":"2 dk","fa":"۲ دقیقه"}}],"context":{"eyebrow":{"en":"1 The context","tr":"1 Bağlam","fa":"۱ بافت"},"head":{"en":"This exam: rice, a determined person, winning","tr":"Bu sınav: pirinç, kararlı biri, kazanmak","fa":"این آزمون: برنج، یک آدم مصمم، برنده شدن"},"intro":{"en":"The three parts are linked: Part 1 is about you, Part 2 is one person on a card, and Part 3 widens the Part 2 topic. Person cards need character, not appearance: what the person does and why it matters.","tr":"Üç kısım birbirine bağlıdır: Part 1 seninle ilgili, Part 2 karttaki bir kişi ve Part 3, Part 2 konusunu genişletir. Kişi kartları dış görünüş değil karakter ister: kişinin ne yaptığı ve bunun neden önemli olduğu.","fa":"سه بخش به هم وصل‌اند: Part 1 درباره‌ی خودت است، Part 2 یک آدم روی کارت و Part 3 موضوع Part 2 را گسترش می‌دهد. کارت‌های آدم شخصیت می‌خواهند، نه ظاهر: آن آدم چه می‌کند و چرا مهم است."},"technique":{"en":"2 The technique","tr":"2 Teknik","fa":"۲ تکنیک"},"labels":{"asks":{"en":"What this part is about","tr":"Bu kısım ne hakkında","fa":"این بخش درباره‌ی چیست"},"fields":{"en":"Headings you will see","tr":"Göreceğin başlıklar","fa":"عنوان‌هایی که می‌بینی"},"words":{"en":"Words that carry the answers","tr":"Cevabı taşıyan kelimeler","fa":"کلمه‌هایی که جواب را می‌آورند"},"a":{"en":"On the paper","tr":"Kâğıtta","fa":"روی برگه"},"b":{"en":"What you hear or read","tr":"Duyduğun ya da okuduğun","fa":"چیزی که می‌شنوی یا می‌خوانی"},"traps":{"en":"Traps","tr":"Tuzaklar","fa":"دام‌ها"},"example":{"en":"Example","tr":"Örnek","fa":"نمونه"},"ideas":{"en":"Ideas","tr":"Fikirler","fa":"ایده‌ها"}},"cards":[{"id":"x04-s1-ctx","exam":true,"patterns":["S1-frame","S1-food"],"often":{"pattern":"S1-food","n":7,"of":40,"label":{"en":"Comes up often in the real exam: 7 of the last 40 tests","tr":"Gerçek sınavda sık çıkar: son 40 sınavın 7’sinde","fa":"در آزمون واقعی زیاد می‌آید: در ۷ آزمون از ۴۰ آزمونِ اخیر"}},"title":{"en":"Part 1: you, then rice","tr":"Part 1: sen, sonra pirinç","fa":"Part 1: خودت، بعد برنج"},"asks":{"en":"The examiner checks your name and asks about your work, studies or home, then four questions on one everyday topic. Here the topic is rice: how often you eat it, how it is cooked, and whether your habits have changed.","tr":"Sınav görevlisi adını kontrol eder, işini, okulunu ya da evini sorar, sonra günlük bir konuda dört soru sorar. Burada konu pirinç: ne sıklıkla yediğin, nasıl pişirildiği ve alışkanlıklarının değişip değişmediği.","fa":"ممتحن اسمت را چک می‌کند، درباره‌ی کار، درس یا خانه‌ات می‌پرسد و بعد چهار سؤال درباره‌ی یک موضوع روزمره. این‌جا موضوع برنج است: چقدر می‌خوری، چطور پخته می‌شود و آیا عادت‌هایت عوض شده."},"fields":["Work or studies","Home","How often you eat rice","Favourite rice dish","Cooking it","Childhood and now"],"words":[{"a":"a staple","b":"a basic food eaten every day","tr":"temel gıda","fa":"غذای اصلی"},{"a":"a side dish","b":"served with the main dish","tr":"garnitür","fa":"غذای جانبی"},{"a":"fluffy","b":"light and soft","tr":"tane tane, kabarık","fa":"دانه‌دانه و پف‌کرده"},{"a":"sticky","b":"the grains stick together","tr":"yapışkan","fa":"چسبناک"},{"a":"a family recipe","b":"the way my family has always made it","tr":"aile tarifi","fa":"دستور پخت خانوادگی"},{"a":"steam","b":"cook with hot water vapour","tr":"buharda pişirmek","fa":"بخارپز کردن"},{"a":"a special occasion","b":"a celebration / a festival","tr":"özel bir gün","fa":"مناسبت خاص"},{"a":"these days","b":"nowadays / now","tr":"bu günlerde","fa":"این روزها"},{"a":"I tend to","b":"I usually","tr":"genellikle ... yaparım","fa":"معمولاً"},{"a":"to be honest","b":"actually / if I’m truthful","tr":"açıkçası","fa":"راستش"}],"traps":[{"en":"One-word answers: \"Yes, every day.\" Add how or why: what kind, with what, on which occasions?","tr":"Tek kelimelik cevaplar: \"Yes, every day.\" Nasıl ya da neden ekle: ne tür, neyle, hangi durumlarda?","fa":"جواب‌های یک‌کلمه‌ای: «Yes, every day.». بگو چطور یا چرا: چه نوعی، با چه چیزی، در چه مناسبت‌هایی؟"},{"en":"A recipe instead of an answer. \"How do you cook rice?\" needs two or three sentences, not ten steps.","tr":"Cevap yerine tarif. \"Pirinci nasıl pişirirsin?\" on adım değil, iki üç cümle ister.","fa":"دستور پخت به جای جواب. «برنج را چطور می‌پزی؟» دو سه جمله می‌خواهد، نه ده مرحله."}],"example":{"text":"Q: \"Do you eat rice often?\"","item":"Which answer is the right length?","answer":"Yes, almost every day. In my family it’s our main food, usually with a vegetable stew or grilled fish.","why":{"en":"An answer, then what you eat it with: about ten seconds.","tr":"Bir cevap, sonra neyle yediğin: yaklaşık on saniye.","fa":"یک جواب، بعد اینکه با چه می‌خوری: حدود ده ثانیه."}}},{"id":"x04-s2-ctx","exam":true,"patterns":["S2-person","PARA-discuss"],"often":{"pattern":"S2-person","n":6,"of":40,"label":{"en":"Comes up often in the real exam: 6 of the last 40 tests","tr":"Gerçek sınavda sık çıkar: son 40 sınavın 6’sında","fa":"در آزمون واقعی زیاد می‌آید: در ۶ آزمون از ۴۰ آزمونِ اخیر"}},"title":{"en":"Part 2: a person who loves a challenge","tr":"Part 2: zorlukları seven biri","fa":"Part 2: کسی که چالش را دوست دارد"},"asks":{"en":"You get a card about a person you know who loves a challenge. One minute to prepare, then up to two minutes alone. Describe the person, give examples of challenges they took on, and explain what you think of this.","tr":"Tanıdığın ve zorlukları seven biri hakkında bir kart alırsın. Bir dakika hazırlık, sonra iki dakikaya kadar tek başına konuşma. Kişiyi anlat, üstlendiği zorluklardan örnekler ver ve bu konuda ne düşündüğünü açıkla.","fa":"کارتی درباره‌ی کسی می‌گیری که می‌شناسی و چالش را دوست دارد. یک دقیقه آماده شدن، بعد تا دو دقیقه حرف زدن به‌تنهایی. آن آدم را توصیف کن، مثال‌هایی از چالش‌هایی که پذیرفته بیاور و بگو نظرت درباره‌اش چیست."},"fields":["Who the person is","How you know them","Challenges they have taken on","What you think about it"],"words":[{"a":"take on a challenge","b":"decide to do something difficult","tr":"bir zorluğu üstlenmek","fa":"چالشی را پذیرفتن"},{"a":"determined","b":"does not give up","tr":"kararlı","fa":"مصمم"},{"a":"competitive","b":"always wants to win","tr":"rekabetçi","fa":"رقابت‌جو"},{"a":"push yourself","b":"make yourself try harder","tr":"kendini zorlamak","fa":"به خودت فشار آوردن"},{"a":"set a goal","b":"decide what you want to achieve","tr":"hedef koymak","fa":"هدف گذاشتن"},{"a":"out of your comfort zone","b":"doing something new and hard","tr":"konfor alanının dışında","fa":"بیرون از منطقه‌ی امن"},{"a":"I admire","b":"I really respect","tr":"hayranım","fa":"تحسینش می‌کنم"},{"a":"inspiring","b":"makes others want to try","tr":"ilham verici","fa":"الهام‌بخش"},{"a":"stubborn","b":"refuses to change their mind","tr":"inatçı","fa":"لجباز"},{"a":"it pays off","b":"it brings good results","tr":"karşılığını verir","fa":"نتیجه می‌دهد"}],"traps":[{"en":"Describing only appearance. The card is about character and actions: give two concrete examples of challenges.","tr":"Yalnızca dış görünüşü anlatmak. Kart karakter ve davranışlarla ilgili: iki somut zorluk örneği ver.","fa":"فقط توصیف ظاهر. کارت درباره‌ی شخصیت و کارهاست: دو مثال مشخص از چالش‌ها بیاور."},{"en":"No opinion at the end. The last line asks what you think: say whether you admire it, and give a reason or a small doubt.","tr":"Sonda görüş yok. Son satır ne düşündüğünü soruyor: buna hayran olup olmadığını söyle, bir neden ya da küçük bir şüphe ekle.","fa":"نظر نداشتن در آخر. خط آخر می‌پرسد چه فکر می‌کنی: بگو تحسینش می‌کنی یا نه و یک دلیل یا یک تردید کوچک اضافه کن."}],"example":{"text":"Card line: \"what challenges this person has taken on\"","item":"Which sentence gives a concrete example?","answer":"Last year she decided to learn to swim at forty, and six months later she swam across the lake near our village.","why":{"en":"A real action, a time and a result: much better than \"she likes hard things\".","tr":"Gerçek bir eylem, bir zaman ve bir sonuç: \"zor şeyleri sever\"den çok daha iyi.","fa":"یک کار واقعی، یک زمان و یک نتیجه: خیلی بهتر از «کارهای سخت را دوست دارد»."}}},{"id":"x04-s3-ctx","exam":true,"patterns":["S3-education","PARA-discuss","TR-short"],"often":{"pattern":"S3-education","n":7,"of":40,"label":{"en":"Comes up often in the real exam: 7 of the last 40 tests","tr":"Gerçek sınavda sık çıkar: son 40 sınavın 7’sinde","fa":"در آزمون واقعی زیاد می‌آید: در ۷ آزمون از ۴۰ آزمونِ اخیر"}},"title":{"en":"Part 3: competitions, prizes and winning","tr":"Part 3: yarışmalar, ödüller ve kazanmak","fa":"Part 3: مسابقه، جایزه و برنده شدن"},"asks":{"en":"The examiner asks six general questions linked to the Part 2 topic: competition in schools and among children, and prizes, taking part and winning in adult life.","tr":"Sınav görevlisi Part 2 konusuyla bağlantılı altı genel soru sorar: okullarda ve çocuklar arasında rekabet, yetişkin hayatında ödüller, katılmak ve kazanmak.","fa":"ممتحن شش سؤال کلی مرتبط با موضوع Part 2 می‌پرسد: رقابت در مدرسه و بین بچه‌ها و جایزه، شرکت کردن و برنده شدن در زندگی بزرگسالی."},"fields":["Competition at school","Children and winning","Team games","Prizes","TV competitions","Taking part or winning"],"words":[{"a":"healthy competition","b":"competition that motivates people","tr":"sağlıklı rekabet","fa":"رقابت سالم"},{"a":"motivate","b":"make someone want to try","tr":"motive etmek","fa":"انگیزه دادن"},{"a":"self-confidence","b":"believing in yourself","tr":"özgüven","fa":"اعتمادبه‌نفس"},{"a":"a sense of achievement","b":"feeling proud of what you did","tr":"başarı duygusu","fa":"حس موفقیت"},{"a":"a reward","b":"something given for doing well","tr":"ödül","fa":"پاداش"},{"a":"teamwork","b":"working together","tr":"takım çalışması","fa":"کار گروهی"},{"a":"a sore loser","b":"someone who gets angry when they lose","tr":"kaybetmeyi kaldıramayan","fa":"بازنده‌ی بداخلاق"},{"a":"take part","b":"join in / participate","tr":"katılmak","fa":"شرکت کردن"},{"a":"on the one hand","b":"from one point of view","tr":"bir yandan","fa":"از یک طرف"},{"a":"it depends on","b":"it varies with","tr":"... bağlıdır","fa":"بستگی دارد به"}],"traps":[{"en":"A one-sentence opinion. Part 3 wants a view, a reason, an example and, when it helps, the other side.","tr":"Tek cümlelik bir görüş. Part 3 bir görüş, bir neden, bir örnek ve gerektiğinde karşı tarafı ister.","fa":"نظری در یک جمله. Part 3 یک نظر، یک دلیل، یک مثال و هرجا لازم بود طرف مقابل را می‌خواهد."},{"en":"Only your own school days. \"Is competition good for children?\" is about children in general; your memory can be one example, not the whole answer.","tr":"Yalnızca kendi okul günlerin. \"Rekabet çocuklar için iyi mi?\" sorusu genel olarak çocuklarla ilgili; anın bir örnek olabilir, cevabın tamamı değil.","fa":"فقط خاطرات مدرسه‌ی خودت. «آیا رقابت برای بچه‌ها خوب است؟» درباره‌ی بچه‌ها به‌طور کلی است؛ خاطره‌ات می‌تواند یک مثال باشد، نه کل جواب."}],"example":{"text":"Q: \"Should schools give prizes to the best students?\"","item":"Which answer has a view, a reason and an example?","answer":"Sometimes, yes, because prizes can motivate pupils to work harder. For example, a reading prize can encourage children who rarely open a book.","why":{"en":"View (sometimes, yes), reason (motivation), example (a reading prize).","tr":"Görüş (bazen, evet), neden (motivasyon), örnek (okuma ödülü).","fa":"نظر (گاهی، بله)، دلیل (انگیزه)، مثال (جایزه‌ی کتاب‌خوانی)."}}},{"id":"S2-person","ctx":["S2-person"],"title":{"en":"A person","tr":"Bir kişi","fa":"یک آدم"},"asks":{"en":"A card about a person: someone competitive, a prize winner, a good friend, a famous businessperson, the founder of a company, a popular actor. The prompts ask who it is, how you know them, what they are like, and why you admire or remember them.","tr":"Bir kişi hakkında kart: rekabetçi biri, ödül kazanan biri, iyi bir arkadaş, ünlü bir iş insanı, bir şirketin kurucusu, sevilen bir oyuncu. Maddeler kim olduğunu, onu nasıl tanıdığını, nasıl biri olduğunu ve ona neden hayran olduğunu ya da neden hatırladığını sorar.","fa":"کارتی درباره‌ی یک آدم: کسی رقابت‌جو، برنده‌ی یک جایزه، یک دوست خوب، یک تاجر مشهور، بنیان‌گذار یک شرکت، یک بازیگر محبوب. بندها می‌پرسند کیست، از کجا می‌شناسی‌اش، چطور آدمی است و چرا تحسینش می‌کنی یا یادت مانده."},"fields":["Describe a person who is very competitive.","Describe a friend you have known for a long time.","Describe someone famous you would like to meet.","Describe a person who won a prize.","Describe a businessperson you admire."],"words":[{"a":"nice","b":"kind / generous / easy-going","tr":"iyi kalpli, cömert","fa":"مهربان، دست‌ودل‌باز"},{"a":"clever","b":"bright / sharp","tr":"zeki","fa":"باهوش"},{"a":"works hard","b":"hard-working / determined","tr":"çalışkan, kararlı","fa":"سخت‌کوش، مصمم"},{"a":"funny","b":"has a great sense of humour","tr":"esprili","fa":"بامزه، شوخ‌طبع"},{"a":"wants to win","b":"competitive / hates losing","tr":"rekabetçi","fa":"رقابت‌جو"},{"a":"famous","b":"well known / a household name","tr":"herkesin tanıdığı","fa":"سرشناس"},{"a":"I met him","b":"I first got to know him when","tr":"onu ilk ... tanıdım","fa":"اولین بار وقتی ... با او آشنا شدم"},{"a":"we are close","b":"we get on really well","tr":"çok iyi anlaşıyoruz","fa":"خیلی با هم جوریم"},{"a":"I respect","b":"I've always admired","tr":"hep hayran olmuşumdur","fa":"همیشه تحسینش کرده‌ام"},{"a":"he helped me","b":"he was there for me when","tr":"... -diğinde yanımdaydı","fa":"وقتی ... کنارم بود"},{"a":"successful","b":"has achieved a great deal","tr":"çok şey başardı","fa":"خیلی موفق بوده"},{"a":"made me want to","b":"inspired me to","tr":"bana ... için ilham verdi","fa":"الهام‌بخش من شد برای"}],"traps":[{"en":"Adjectives alone (\"kind, funny, clever\") run out in twenty seconds. One story that shows the quality lasts a minute.","tr":"Yalnızca sıfatlar (\"kind, funny, clever\") yirmi saniyede tükenir. O niteliği gösteren bir hikâye bir dakika sürer.","fa":"فقط صفت‌ها («kind، funny، clever») در بیست ثانیه تمام می‌شوند. یک داستان که آن ویژگی را نشان دهد یک دقیقه طول می‌کشد."},{"en":"A famous person you have not met: say how you know about them (an interview, a book, a film).","tr":"Hiç tanışmadığın ünlü biri: onu nereden bildiğini söyle (bir röportaj, bir kitap, bir film).","fa":"آدم مشهوری که هیچ‌وقت ندیده‌ای: بگو از کجا درباره‌اش می‌دانی (یک مصاحبه، یک کتاب، یک فیلم)."}],"example":{"lines":[["Candidate","My friend Deniz is the most competitive person I know."],["Candidate","Once we played a board game at a family party, and when he lost, he insisted on playing again until midnight."],["Candidate","It sounds funny now, but the same attitude helped him get into a top university."]],"item":"What makes this description work?","answer":"A quality, then a short story that shows it, then a link to a result.","why":{"en":"The story proves the adjective and gives the talk something to grow from.","tr":"Hikâye sıfatı kanıtlıyor ve konuşmaya büyüyecek bir zemin veriyor.","fa":"داستان صفت را ثابت می‌کند و به صحبت زمینه‌ای برای ادامه می‌دهد."}},"ideas":["how you know this person","one story that shows their character","what they look like (briefly)","what other people think of them","why you admire them (explain)"],"general":true,"patterns":["S2-person"],"often":{"pattern":"S2-person","n":6,"of":40,"label":{"en":"Comes up often in the real exam: 6 of the last 40 tests","tr":"Gerçek sınavda sık çıkar: son 40 sınavın 6’sında","fa":"در آزمون واقعی زیاد می‌آید: در ۶ آزمون از ۴۰ آزمونِ اخیر"}}},{"id":"S3-education","ctx":["S3-education"],"title":{"en":"Education, children and family","tr":"Eğitim, çocuklar ve aile","fa":"آموزش، کودکان و خانواده"},"asks":{"en":"General questions linked to the Part 2 card, about school rules, rewarding children, cooking at school, family gatherings, friendship and children’s books. The examiner wants an opinion, a reason, an example and, when it helps, the other side.","tr":"Part 2 kartına bağlı, okul kuralları, çocukları ödüllendirmek, okulda yemek pişirmek, aile toplantıları, arkadaşlık ve çocuk kitapları hakkında genel sorular. Sınav görevlisi bir görüş, bir neden, bir örnek ve gerektiğinde karşı tarafı ister.","fa":"سؤال‌های کلی مرتبط با کارت Part 2، درباره‌ی قانون‌های مدرسه، تشویق بچه‌ها، آشپزی در مدرسه، دورهمی‌های خانوادگی، دوستی و کتاب‌های کودکان. ممتحن یک نظر، یک دلیل، یک مثال و هرجا لازم بود طرف مقابل را می‌خواهد."},"fields":["Should children be rewarded for good behaviour?","Should schools teach cooking?","Are family gatherings less common than in the past?","Do children read less than before?","Should music and art be taught at school?"],"words":[{"a":"children","b":"youngsters / kids","tr":"çocuklar","fa":"بچه‌ها"},{"a":"parents","b":"mothers and fathers / families","tr":"ebeveynler","fa":"والدین"},{"a":"rules","b":"discipline","tr":"disiplin","fa":"انضباط"},{"a":"give a prize","b":"reward / praise","tr":"ödüllendirmek","fa":"تشویق کردن"},{"a":"punish","b":"discipline / take something away","tr":"cezalandırmak","fa":"تنبیه کردن"},{"a":"life skills","b":"practical skills like cooking","tr":"yaşam becerileri","fa":"مهارت‌های زندگی"},{"a":"creative","b":"imaginative","tr":"yaratıcı","fa":"خلاق"},{"a":"get together","b":"family gatherings","tr":"aile buluşmaları","fa":"دورهمی‌های خانوادگی"},{"a":"grow up","b":"develop / mature","tr":"büyümek, olgunlaşmak","fa":"بزرگ شدن"},{"a":"screens","b":"tablets and phones","tr":"ekranlar","fa":"صفحه‌نمایش‌ها"},{"a":"in the past","b":"when my parents were young","tr":"ebeveynlerim gençken","fa":"وقتی پدر و مادرم جوان بودند"},{"a":"nowadays","b":"these days","tr":"günümüzde","fa":"این روزها"}],"traps":[{"en":"Past-and-present questions need two tenses: \"used to\" for the past, present simple for now.","tr":"Geçmiş ve şimdi soruları iki zaman ister: geçmiş için \"used to\", şimdi için geniş zaman.","fa":"سؤال‌های گذشته و حال دو زمان می‌خواهند: «used to» برای گذشته، حال ساده برای حالا."},{"en":"Give a balanced answer when people really disagree: show you know both sides.","tr":"İnsanlar gerçekten farklı düşünüyorsa dengeli cevap ver: iki tarafı da bildiğini göster.","fa":"وقتی مردم واقعاً نظر متفاوت دارند، جواب متعادل بده: نشان بده هر دو طرف را می‌دانی."}],"example":{"lines":[["Examiner","Are family gatherings less common than they used to be?"],["Candidate","In my country, yes, a little. People used to meet every weekend at their grandparents’ house."],["Candidate","Nowadays families are often spread across different cities, so they meet mainly on holidays, although they talk online almost every day."]],"item":"How does the speaker compare past and present?","answer":"\"Used to\" for the past habit, present simple with \"nowadays\" for today, and a reason (families are spread out).","why":{"en":"Two tenses and a time word make the comparison clear.","tr":"İki zaman ve bir zaman kelimesi karşılaştırmayı netleştiriyor.","fa":"دو زمان و یک قید زمان مقایسه را روشن می‌کنند."}},"ideas":["praise works better than prizes","cooking teaches health and independence","families are busier but meet online","children read differently, not less"],"general":true,"patterns":["S3-education"],"often":{"pattern":"S3-education","n":7,"of":40,"label":{"en":"Comes up often in the real exam: 7 of the last 40 tests","tr":"Gerçek sınavda sık çıkar: son 40 sınavın 7’sinde","fa":"در آزمون واقعی زیاد می‌آید: در ۷ آزمون از ۴۰ آزمونِ اخیر"}}}]},"points":[{"eyebrow":{"en":"In the exam","tr":"Sınavda","fa":"در آزمون"},"head":{"en":"Three parts, one examiner","tr":"Üç kısım, bir sınav görevlisi","fa":"سه بخش، یک ممتحن"},"body":{"en":"Part 1 (4-5 minutes): questions about you and one everyday topic. Part 2 (3-4 minutes): one minute to prepare, then up to two minutes alone, then one short question. Part 3 (4-5 minutes): a discussion of general questions. The test is recorded.","tr":"Part 1 (4-5 dakika): seninle ve günlük bir konuyla ilgili sorular. Part 2 (3-4 dakika): bir dakika hazırlık, sonra iki dakikaya kadar tek başına konuşma, sonra kısa bir soru. Part 3 (4-5 dakika): genel soruların tartışması. Sınav kaydedilir.","fa":"Part 1 (۴ تا ۵ دقیقه): سؤال‌هایی درباره‌ی خودت و یک موضوع روزمره. Part 2 (۳ تا ۴ دقیقه): یک دقیقه آماده شدن، بعد تا دو دقیقه حرف زدن به‌تنهایی و بعد یک سؤال کوتاه. Part 3 (۴ تا ۵ دقیقه): بحث درباره‌ی سؤال‌های کلی. آزمون ضبط می‌شود."}},{"eyebrow":{"en":"The method","tr":"Yöntem","fa":"روش"},"head":{"en":"Show the person through stories","tr":"Kişiyi hikâyelerle göster","fa":"آدم را با داستان نشان بده"},"steps":[{"en":"Part 1: answer, then add one detail: when, with what, or why.","tr":"Part 1: cevap ver, sonra bir ayrıntı ekle: ne zaman, neyle ya da neden.","fa":"Part 1: جواب بده و بعد یک جزئیات اضافه کن: کی، با چه، یا چرا."},{"en":"Part 2: say who and how you know them, then tell two short stories that show the challenges they took on.","tr":"Part 2: kim olduğunu ve onu nereden tanıdığını söyle, sonra üstlendiği zorlukları gösteren iki kısa hikâye anlat.","fa":"Part 2: بگو کیست و از کجا می‌شناسی‌اش، بعد دو داستان کوتاه بگو که چالش‌هایی را که پذیرفته نشان می‌دهند."},{"en":"Part 3: give a view, a reason and an example, then the other side if it helps.","tr":"Part 3: bir görüş, bir neden ve bir örnek ver; gerekiyorsa karşı tarafı da söyle.","fa":"Part 3: یک نظر، یک دلیل و یک مثال بده و اگر کمک می‌کند طرف مقابل را هم بگو."}]},{"eyebrow":{"en":"The trap","tr":"Tuzak","fa":"دام"},"head":{"en":"Adjectives without examples","tr":"Örneksiz sıfatlar","fa":"صفت بدون مثال"},"body":{"en":"Saying \"she is brave, determined and competitive\" takes ten seconds and proves nothing. One real example of something the person did is worth more than five adjectives, and it fills the two minutes naturally.","tr":"\"Cesur, kararlı ve rekabetçi\" demek on saniye sürer ve hiçbir şey kanıtlamaz. Kişinin yaptığı gerçek bir şeyin tek bir örneği beş sıfattan değerlidir ve iki dakikayı doğal biçimde doldurur.","fa":"گفتنِ «شجاع، مصمم و رقابت‌جوست» ده ثانیه طول می‌کشد و چیزی را ثابت نمی‌کند. یک مثال واقعی از کاری که آن آدم کرده از پنج صفت ارزشمندتر است و دو دقیقه را طبیعی پر می‌کند."}}],"example":{"eyebrow":{"en":"Worked example","tr":"Çözümlü örnek","fa":"مثال حل‌شده"},"head":{"en":"Planning a person talk in one minute","tr":"Bir dakikada bir kişi konuşması planlamak","fa":"برنامه‌ریزی صحبت درباره‌ی یک آدم در یک دقیقه"},"instruction":"Card: Describe a person you know who is very patient. You should say: who this person is; how you know them; what they do that shows their patience; and explain how you feel about this person.","item":"Write one key word for each line.","answer":"grandfather · summers at his farm · taught me to fish, never angry · calm → I try to copy him","walk":[{"en":"Who and how: a short note for each.","tr":"Kim ve nereden: her biri için kısa bir not.","fa":"چه کسی و از کجا: برای هر کدام یک یادداشت کوتاه."},{"en":"Choose one memory that shows the quality: teaching you to fish.","tr":"Bu özelliği gösteren bir anı seç: sana balık tutmayı öğretmesi.","fa":"یک خاطره انتخاب کن که آن ویژگی را نشان بدهد: یاد دادن ماهیگیری به تو."},{"en":"Note your feeling for the last line: you try to copy him.","tr":"Son satır için duygunu not et: onu örnek almaya çalışıyorsun.","fa":"احساست را برای خط آخر یادداشت کن: سعی می‌کنی مثل او باشی."}]},"quick":{"prompt":"Part 3: \"Is competition good for children?\" Which answer is about children in general?","options":["I won a race when I was eight.","Yes.","In moderation, yes: it can teach children to try hard, as long as adults don’t make losing feel like a disaster."],"correct":2,"why":{"en":"It gives a view about children in general, a reason and a condition; the others are about the speaker or too short.","tr":"Genel olarak çocuklar hakkında bir görüş, bir neden ve bir koşul veriyor; diğerleri konuşanla ilgili ya da çok kısa.","fa":"درباره‌ی بچه‌ها به‌طور کلی نظر، دلیل و شرط می‌دهد؛ بقیه درباره‌ی خود گوینده‌اند یا خیلی کوتاه‌اند."}},"remember":{"en":"Part 1: answer plus a detail. Part 2: show the person through real examples. Part 3: view, reason, example.","tr":"Part 1: cevap artı bir ayrıntı. Part 2: kişiyi gerçek örneklerle göster. Part 3: görüş, neden, örnek.","fa":"Part 1: جواب به‌اضافه‌ی یک جزئیات. Part 2: آدم را با مثال‌های واقعی نشان بده. Part 3: نظر، دلیل، مثال."},"type":"explain","id":"c-x04-s-e","course":"ielts-exams","exam":"exam-04","unit":"x04-s"},"sets":{"title":{"en":"The Speaking test","tr":"Speaking sınavı","fa":"آزمون Speaking"},"note":{"en":"Do the three parts in order, without a break, as in the real test. Record yourself if you can, then use the self-check under each part.","tr":"Gerçek sınavdaki gibi üç kısmı sırayla ve ara vermeden yap. Yapabilirsen kendini kaydet, sonra her kısmın altındaki öz değerlendirmeyi kullan.","fa":"سه بخش را به ترتیب و بدون مکث انجام بده، مثل آزمون واقعی. اگر می‌توانی صدایت را ضبط کن و بعد از خودارزیابیِ زیر هر بخش استفاده کن."},"sequential":true,"examinerVoice":{"accent":"British (standard Southern)","gender":"M","tts":{"engine":"kokoro","voice":"bm_lewis"},"role":"Examiner"},"sets":[{"part":"Part 1","ctx":["S1-frame","S1-food"],"minutes":[4,5],"title":{"en":"Part 1: about you, then rice","tr":"Part 1: senin hakkında, sonra pirinç","fa":"Part 1: درباره‌ی خودت، بعد برنج"},"examinerIntro":["Good morning. My name is Peter Ashworth. Can you tell me your full name, please?","Thank you. And can I see your identification, please?","Thank you. Now, in this first part, I’d like to ask you some questions about yourself."],"frame":["Do you work or are you a student?","Do you get on well with the people you work or study with?","Let’s talk about your home town. What is it known for?"],"topicIntro":"Now let’s talk about rice.","questions":["How often do you eat rice?","What is your favourite dish with rice in it?","Did you eat more rice when you were a child than you do now?","Is rice an important part of meals for special occasions in your country?"],"model":"Q: How often do you eat rice?\nA: Almost every day, to be honest. In my family it’s a staple, so we usually have it at dinner with a vegetable stew or some grilled chicken.\n\nQ: What is your favourite dish with rice in it?\nA: Probably a rice dish my aunt makes with herbs, broad beans and dill. It smells wonderful, and she always makes far too much, so there’s some left for the next day.\n\nQ: Did you eat more rice as a child?\nA: I think I did. My grandmother lived with us and cooked rice twice a day. These days I eat more bread and pasta, because they’re quicker to prepare after work.\n\nQ: Is rice important for special occasions?\nA: Very. At weddings and big family celebrations, there’s always a huge dish of rice in the middle of the table, often decorated with nuts and saffron.","moves":[{"label":{"en":"Answer first","tr":"Önce cevap","fa":"اول جواب"},"example":"Almost every day, to be honest."},{"label":{"en":"Add a detail: what with, who, when","tr":"Bir ayrıntı ekle: neyle, kim, ne zaman","fa":"یک جزئیات اضافه کن: با چه، چه کسی، کی"},"example":"We usually have it at dinner with a vegetable stew or some grilled chicken."},{"label":{"en":"A then/now contrast","tr":"O zaman/şimdi karşıtlığı","fa":"تضاد «آن موقع/حالا»"},"example":"My grandmother cooked rice twice a day. These days I eat more bread and pasta."}],"selfCheck":[{"en":"I answered every question with two or three sentences, not one word.","tr":"Her soruyu tek kelimeyle değil, iki üç cümleyle cevapladım.","fa":"به هر سؤال با دو سه جمله جواب دادم، نه یک کلمه."},{"en":"I described food with real details, not a long recipe.","tr":"Yemeği uzun bir tarifle değil, gerçek ayrıntılarla anlattım.","fa":"غذا را با جزئیات واقعی توصیف کردم، نه با یک دستور پخت طولانی."},{"en":"I used the past for my childhood and the present for now.","tr":"Çocukluğum için geçmiş, şimdi için geniş zaman kullandım.","fa":"برای کودکی گذشته و برای الان حال را به کار بردم."}]},{"part":"Part 2","ctx":["S2-person"],"minutes":[3,4],"title":{"en":"Part 2: a person who loves a challenge","tr":"Part 2: zorlukları seven biri","fa":"Part 2: کسی که چالش را دوست دارد"},"examinerIntro":["Now I’m going to give you a topic, and I’d like you to talk about it for one to two minutes. Before you talk, you’ll have one minute to think about what you’re going to say. You can make some notes if you wish. Do you understand?","Here’s some paper and a pencil for making notes, and here’s your topic. I’d like you to describe a person you know who loves a challenge.","All right? Remember you have one to two minutes for this. Don’t worry if I stop you. I’ll tell you when the time is up. Can you start speaking now, please?"],"card":{"task":"Describe a person you know who loves a challenge.","bullets":["who this person is","how you know this person","what challenges this person has taken on","and explain what you think about this person’s attitude to challenges"]},"prep":60,"talk":120,"roundingOff":["Do you enjoy challenges yourself?"],"model":"I’d like to talk about my friend Noor, who I’ve known since we were at secondary school together. We were in the same class for six years, and although we now live in different cities, we still speak every week.\n\nNoor is one of those people who can’t say no to a challenge. At school, when our teacher mentioned a national science competition, she was the only person in our class who entered. She spent every lunch break for two months building a little water filter out of sand and charcoal, and she came third in the whole country.\n\nThe biggest challenge she has taken on, though, came much later. Three years ago she decided to run a marathon, even though at that time she couldn’t run for more than ten minutes without stopping. She found a training plan online, got up at six every morning, and kept a notebook of every run. Some days she was exhausted, and once she hurt her knee, but she simply changed her plan and carried on. She finished the race in just under five hours, and the photo of her crossing the line is still on her phone.\n\nWhat do I think of her attitude? Mostly, I really admire it. She shows that you don’t have to be naturally talented to achieve something; you just have to keep going. Sometimes I think she takes on too much and gets very tired, and I’ve told her so. But she always says that a challenge that feels easy isn’t worth doing, and to be honest, she has inspired me to try a few things myself.","moves":[{"label":{"en":"Who and how you know them","tr":"Kim ve nereden tanıdığın","fa":"چه کسی و از کجا می‌شناسی‌اش"},"example":"I’d like to talk about my friend Noor, who I’ve known since we were at secondary school together."},{"label":{"en":"Two real challenges, as short stories","tr":"Kısa hikâyeler olarak iki gerçek zorluk","fa":"دو چالش واقعی، به شکل داستان کوتاه"},"example":"At school... she came third in the whole country... Three years ago she decided to run a marathon..."},{"label":{"en":"Your view, with a small doubt","tr":"Görüşün, küçük bir şüpheyle","fa":"نظرت، با یک تردید کوچک"},"example":"Mostly, I really admire it... Sometimes I think she takes on too much..."}],"selfCheck":[{"en":"I covered all four lines of the card and spoke for close to two minutes.","tr":"Kartın dört satırının hepsini ele aldım ve iki dakikaya yakın konuştum.","fa":"هر چهار خط کارت را گفتم و نزدیک دو دقیقه حرف زدم."},{"en":"I gave at least two concrete examples, not just adjectives.","tr":"Yalnızca sıfatlar değil, en az iki somut örnek verdim.","fa":"دست‌کم دو مثال مشخص دادم، نه فقط صفت."},{"en":"I gave my own opinion of the person at the end.","tr":"Sonda kişi hakkında kendi görüşümü verdim.","fa":"در آخر نظر خودم را درباره‌ی آن آدم گفتم."}]},{"part":"Part 3","ctx":["S3-education"],"minutes":[4,5],"title":{"en":"Part 3: competitions, prizes and winning","tr":"Part 3: yarışmalar, ödüller ve kazanmak","fa":"Part 3: مسابقه، جایزه و برنده شدن"},"examinerIntro":["We’ve been talking about a person who loves a challenge, and I’d like to discuss with you one or two more general questions related to this."],"subtopics":[{"title":"Competition and children","questions":["Is it good for children to compete against each other at school?","Should schools give prizes to the best pupils, or reward effort instead?","How can parents help children to deal with losing?"]},{"title":"Prizes and winning","questions":["Why are television competitions with big prizes so popular?","Is taking part more important than winning?","Do you think people today are more competitive than in the past?"]}],"model":"Q: Should schools give prizes to the best pupils, or reward effort instead?\nA: I think schools should reward effort at least as much as results. If prizes only go to the top students, the same few children win every year, and the others simply stop trying. A good example is a \"most improved\" award, which gives a weaker student something realistic to aim for. That said, I don’t think we should hide excellence completely, because high achievers need motivation too.\n\nQ: Is taking part more important than winning?\nA: For most people, yes, especially in amateur sport. You get fitness, friends and a sense of achievement whether you win or not. In professional sport it’s different, of course: winning is the job. But even there, the athletes who last longest are often the ones who enjoy the game itself, not just the medals.","moves":[{"label":{"en":"Give a clear view","tr":"Net bir görüş ver","fa":"نظرت را روشن بگو"},"example":"I think schools should reward effort at least as much as results."},{"label":{"en":"Support it: reason + example","tr":"Destekle: neden + örnek","fa":"پشتیبانی کن: دلیل + مثال"},"example":"If prizes only go to the top students, the others simply stop trying. A good example is a \"most improved\" award..."},{"label":{"en":"Show the other side","tr":"Karşı tarafı göster","fa":"طرف مقابل را نشان بده"},"example":"That said, I don’t think we should hide excellence completely..."}],"selfCheck":[{"en":"I gave a clear view in my first sentence.","tr":"İlk cümlemde net bir görüş verdim.","fa":"در جمله‌ی اولم نظر روشنی دادم."},{"en":"I supported it with a reason and an example.","tr":"Onu bir neden ve bir örnekle destekledim.","fa":"آن را با یک دلیل و یک مثال پشتیبانی کردم."},{"en":"I talked about people in general, not only about myself.","tr":"Yalnızca kendimden değil, genel olarak insanlardan söz ettim.","fa":"درباره‌ی آدم‌ها به‌طور کلی حرف زدم، نه فقط خودم."}]}],"type":"sets","id":"c-x04-s-p","course":"ielts-exams","exam":"exam-04","unit":"x04-s"},"exit":{"type":"exit","items":[{"tests":"word","point":1,"prompt":"\"Rice is a staple in my country.\" A staple is...","options":["a food for special occasions","a basic food eaten very often","an expensive food"],"correct":1,"why":{"en":"A staple = a main food that people eat regularly.","tr":"Staple = insanların düzenli yediği temel gıda.","fa":"staple یعنی غذای اصلی که مردم مرتب می‌خورند."}},{"tests":"paraphrase","point":2,"prompt":"Which phrase means \"decide to do something difficult\"?","options":["take on a challenge","give up a challenge","avoid a challenge"],"correct":0,"why":{"en":"To take on = to accept a task or challenge.","tr":"Take on = bir görevi ya da zorluğu üstlenmek.","fa":"take on یعنی پذیرفتن یک کار یا چالش."}},{"tests":"method","point":2,"prompt":"Your Part 2 card is about a person. After thirty seconds you have listed four adjectives. What should you do next?","options":["List more adjectives","Describe what the person looks like","Tell a short story that shows one of the qualities"],"correct":2,"why":{"en":"A real example shows the quality and fills the time; more adjectives do not.","tr":"Gerçek bir örnek özelliği gösterir ve süreyi doldurur; daha fazla sıfat bunu yapmaz.","fa":"یک مثال واقعی ویژگی را نشان می‌دهد و وقت را پر می‌کند؛ صفت بیشتر نه."}},{"tests":"trap","point":3,"prompt":"Part 3: \"Is taking part more important than winning?\" Which answer has the most complete structure?","options":["Yes, definitely.","For most people, yes: you gain fitness and friends either way, although in professional sport winning is the job.","I came last in a race once and I didn’t mind."],"correct":1,"why":{"en":"A view, reasons and the other side; the last answer is only about the speaker.","tr":"Bir görüş, nedenler ve karşı taraf; son cevap yalnızca konuşanla ilgili.","fa":"یک نظر، دلیل‌ها و طرف مقابل؛ جواب آخر فقط درباره‌ی گوینده است."}},{"tests":"trap","point":1,"prompt":"Part 1: \"How do you usually cook rice?\" Which answer is the right length?","options":["I usually boil it with a little salt and then let it steam for ten minutes, so it comes out fluffy.","Boil.","First you wash it three times, then you soak it, then you measure the water, then..."],"correct":0,"why":{"en":"Part 1 wants two or three natural sentences, not one word and not a full recipe.","tr":"Part 1 tek kelime ya da tam bir tarif değil, iki üç doğal cümle ister.","fa":"Part 1 دو سه جمله‌ی طبیعی می‌خواهد، نه یک کلمه و نه یک دستور پخت کامل."}}],"id":"c-x04-s-x","course":"ielts-exams","exam":"exam-04","unit":"x04-s"}}; })(globalThis.IELTS_EXAMS = globalThis.IELTS_EXAMS || {});
